# =============================================================================
#  WHAT NEVER GOES INTO THE IMAGE
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Two kinds of thing are excluded here, and only one of them is about size.
#
#  The first is SECRETS AND THE SHOP'S OWN DATA. server/data/ holds og.db —
#  real customers, real sales, real sealed passwords — and server/data/certs/
#  holds a private key. server/.env holds the Supabase service key, both
#  Telegram tokens and OG_VAULT_KEY. An image is a file anybody who can pull
#  it can unpack; none of this may ever be baked into one. The database
#  arrives at run time on a volume, the keys as environment variables.
#
#  The second is EVERYTHING THAT CANNOT RUN IN A CONTAINER ANYWAY: the Windows
#  launcher, the print agent, the test harnesses, the Flutter port, the docs.
# =============================================================================

# ---- the shop's data and its keys -------------------------------------------
server/data/
server/data-sandbox/
server/data-sandbox2/
server/backups/
server/.env
server/.env.*
ACCOUNTS.private.md

# ---- git, CI and editor -----------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.claude/
.serena/
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---- the Windows launcher and the print agent -------------------------------
#  panel/ is a tray application for the shop's laptop and the .exe it builds;
#  agent/ talks to a USB label printer. Neither has anything to reach from a
#  VPS, and both would only be weight.
panel/
agent/
*.exe
*.bat
*.ps1

# ---- test harnesses and scratch ---------------------------------------------
#  Files starting with `_` are refused by serveStatic anyway (lib/http.js);
#  keeping them out of the image means they are not there to refuse.
_nightshift/
_*.html
*.log
*.tmp

# ---- things that are not the app --------------------------------------------
dist/
flutter_app/
docs/
*.md
!server/README.md

# ---- docker's own ------------------------------------------------------------
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
